Forwarding Daytona's latest public announcement, summarized for diligence.

Daytona has raised a $24M Series A led by FirstMark Capital (February 5, 2026), with participation from Pace Capital and existing investors Upfront Ventures, E2VC and Darkmode. Datadog and Figma Ventures made strategic investments.
Matt Turck, General Partner at FirstMark, has joined the Daytona Board of Directors.
Daytona is a 20-person team.
Daytona reached a $1M forward revenue run rate in under three months. Six weeks later, it doubled.
Customers include LangChain, Turing, Writer, and SambaNova.
The Series A brings Daytona's total funding to $31M, per CEO Ivan Burazin.
Daytona was founded in 2023 by Ivan Burazin (CEO), Vedran Jukic (CTO), and Goran Draganic (Chief Architect).
Daytona is based in New York.

